iff PASS; exact shellcheck/zizmor/predates-gate-ok/mechanism-ok text and next-code attachment PASS\n- Focused verification: 24 + 78 + 25 + 170 = 297 passed; 3 expected skips\n- Additional checks: comment hygiene PASS; path-scoped diff check PASS; verify-commit-ticket PASS; worktree-venv make lint/actionlint/zizmor PASS\n- User-authorized substitution: did not run make verify/full test suite for this comments-only session; Gerrit Verified CI is the full-suite oracle\n- Attempts/defects: two prose-edit validation cycles; one semantic documentation defect found by focused tests (literal INCLUDED/NO_FILTER trigger classifications), fixed and revalidated; first commit attempt rejected by 50/72 message gate, second passed; one verify-commit-ticket syntax retry (--rev)\n- DCO, Change-Id, and canonical rebar-ticket trailer present\n- Pending: independent non-author TSV review, Gerrit push/votes/submit, completion verification, close","timestamp":1788819055644093236}],"created_at":1788570426598474267,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"359e3125-143b-4171-b15a-fed9a9e2ed68","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"67b3-e6c3-7bdd-41be"},{"link_uuid":"a0482ec0-ebbd-4323-a2f3-471dd778cd8d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"413d-3bba-ae33-4e3b"},{"link_uuid":"0690050a-6504-4a61-aed3-0a015830933c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"7017-d1ee-5992-4870"},{"link_uuid":"292397d3-1618-473c-a408-c07d9784d7ea","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5e98-6336-e946-47c2"},{"link_uuid":"7d34022b-326d-45e1-8b9b-745e4aee14d1","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"93ba-ee7d-b68b-417d"},{"link_uuid":"d0f6bda4-23ac-42f9-b686-499231b4f8a1","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d8fe-3149-6b2c-430c"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nSix workflow files contain repeated, obvious, historical, or stale prose. Scope was revalidated on `origin/main@d6669496cae4`, including the new named Windows-lock proof in `test.yml`. Shortening comments must preserve trigger, permission, security, portability, and evidence contracts.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only allowlisted standalone comments and adjacent blank lines. Preserve workflow data, embedded shell, expressions, and behavior-bearing directives byte-for-byte. Replace narration with the minimum current rationale needed by each consumer.\n\n## Scope\n- `reconcile-bridge.yml` — Preserve copyable-client semantics; hourly/manual modes; Actions and ref-lock concurrency; full-history tickets worktree with merge-not-rebase/merge driver; job-local permissions; completed-pass-only 60-minute ceiling; pinned acli; temporary signing key/unsigned fallback; fail-loud no-op detection; default-off paced continuous chain with bounded failure handling; and conditional dimensionless CloudWatch metrics that never alter job outcome.\n- `release.yml` — Preserve dispatch-from-main authorization; version/registry/ancestry/environment/advisory guards; immutable pins; build-once artifacts with digest and baked-commit provenance; installed archive tests; exact-byte OIDC PyPI promotion; post-publish tag/release; publisher-digest verification before OIDC; bounded idempotent registry publish; evidence fragments; both `shellcheck disable=SC1091` directives; and the `zizmor` marker.\n- `structured-output-baseline.yml` — Preserve manual canonical-repository billable measurement; pre-call budget refusal; independent provider arms and secrets; Bedrock OIDC with both regions and step-confined exchange; external-test opt-in; provider overlays; 3600-second sweep bound; and always-uploaded unique raw results.\n- `terraform-drift.yml` — Preserve Terraform-path PR plus daily/manual triggers; independent fmt/plan jobs; plan-only OIDC; full-history checkout and current-tree assertion; Terraform 1.11.4 floor; validate-before-plan; detailed exit codes with `-lock=false`; advisory role outside Gerrit Verified; and the exact `mechanism-ok: ci_gate` marker.\n- `test.yml` — Preserve ordinary pushes excluding `feature/**`, `main`, and `tickets`; all PRs; six-hour/manual health; same-ref cancellation; shared Gerrit workflows; schedule-only mutation omission; clean-install path; soft last-green/bisect report; external self-skip behavior; breadth-tier distinctions; nonblocking link check; and the exact existing `predates-gate-ok` marker. For the named Windows exclusive-leg proof, condense the explanatory blocks before the `mechanism-ok` marker and between the step name and `continue-on-error`; preserve the complete `mechanism-ok: ci_gate` marker, if-present guard, bash shell, nonblocking disposition, placement before the default suite, and verbose platform-test command. Do not claim every trigger runs the full suite.\n- `verify-identity.yml` — Preserve config-driven advisory authentication and grandfathering; triggers/exclusions; full-history blobless checkout; temporary fail-closed pack limit with restoration; tickets worktree; ancestry-based key verification; object-database immutability; and config-driven op-cert verification without CI overrides.\n\nConsumers are GitHub Actions, Gerrit Verified, release and Terraform operators, PyPI/MCP Registry/GitHub Releases, Jira/tickets reconciliation, CloudWatch, and repository workflow-policy tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only allowlisted standalone comments or adjacent blank lines change in the six paths; workflow data, embedded shell, and directives remain exact.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and consumer has a concrete before/final PASS citation in a leaf-linked TSV authored by a reviewer who did not write the remediation.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and records `semantic-preservation=PASS` and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing or failing rows block closure.\n- [ ] The comment-only guard, directive census, focused workflow tests, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv repository gate pass.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded comment-only and exact-directive guards, focused workflow suites, path-scoped diff check, and worktree-venv lint. The independe